**Given:**

If {sqrt {2116} } = 46 , then find the value of {sqrt {21.16} } + {sqrt {0.2116} } + {sqrt {0.002116} } + {sqrt {0.00002116} }

**Formula Used:**

sqrt{a times 10ⁿ} = sqrt{a} times 10ⁿ/²

**Calculation:**

sqrt{2116} = 46

sqrt{21.16} = sqrt{2116 times 10⁻²}

⇒ sqrt{2116} times 10⁻¹ = 46 times 10⁻¹ = 4.6

sqrt{0.2116} = sqrt{2116 times 10⁻⁴}

⇒ sqrt{2116} times 10⁻² = 46 times 10⁻² = 0.46

sqrt{0.002116} = sqrt{2116 times 10⁻⁶}

⇒ sqrt{2116} times 10⁻³ = 46 times 10⁻³ = 0.046

sqrt{0.00002116} = sqrt{2116 times 10⁻⁸}

⇒ sqrt{2116} times 10⁻⁴ = 46 times 10⁻⁴ = 0.0046

sqrt{21.16} + sqrt{0.2116} + sqrt{0.002116} + sqrt{0.00002116}

⇒ 4.6 + 0.46 + 0.046 + 0.0046

⇒ 5.1106

